WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.273
Welcome to Model Artifact Integrity and
Safe Promotion. This lesson

2
00:00:04.273 --> 00:00:08.545
treats a model repository as supply-chain
input, not as a

3
00:00:08.545 --> 00:00:12.818
harmless collection of weight files. You
will design a quarantine

4
00:00:12.818 --> 00:00:17.091
boundary, distinguish what each
verification signal proves, inspect

5
00:00:17.091 --> 00:00:21.364
executable and parser surfaces before
loading, give every transformation a

6
00:00:21.364 --> 00:00:25.636
new identity, and promote only a complete
immutable bundle with

7
00:00:25.636 --> 00:00:29.909
a tested revocation path. We will use the
supplied synthetic

8
00:00:29.909 --> 00:00:34.182
manifest and inert fixture. There is no
download, model load,

9
00:00:34.182 --> 00:00:38.455
deserialization, conversion, inference,
serving action, or live provider

10
00:00:38.455 --> 00:00:42.727
integration in this lesson. The observed
results are supplied fixture

11
00:00:42.727 --> 00:00:47.000
evidence, not claims about production
infrastructure.

12
00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:51.500
Start with an exact pinned revision in a
bounded, non-serving

13
00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:56.000
quarantine. The quarantine must not
contain learner data or production

14
00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:00.500
credentials. Give it only the network
access, storage, CPU, memory,

15
00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:05.000
process, and file authority required for
acquisition and inspection. Preserve

16
00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:09.500
original filenames and repository
metadata. Do not enable remote code,

17
00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:14.000
plugins, post-install hooks, automatic
execution, model loading, or conversion

18
00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:18.500
merely to discover package contents.
Before any transformation, record the

19
00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:23.000
authoritative source, immutable revision,
retrieval time, transfer method, expected

20
00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:27.500
inventory, observed inventory, file sizes,
and cryptographic digests. Compare the

21
00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:32.000
expected and observed inventories. A
mutable branch, tag, latest alias,

22
00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:36.500
cache entry, or friendly model name must
not silently replace

23
00:01:36.500 --> 00:01:41.000
the approved revision. Quarantine is a
trust boundary enforced by

24
00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:45.500
isolation and policy. A directory called
quarantine is not sufficient

25
00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:50.000
if it shares serving credentials, runtime
authority, caches, or unrestricted

26
00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:54.500
network access. Files may move from
acquisition into verification, but

27
00:01:54.500 --> 00:01:59.000
they must not enter a trusted runtime
until every required

28
00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:03.500
control reaches pass. Hold means evidence
is incomplete and promotion

29
00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:08.000
pauses. Reject means a control failed and
serving remains blocked.

30
00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:12.462
Consider a synthetic package whose
expected inventory contains two weight

31
00:02:12.462 --> 00:02:16.923
shards, one tokenizer, one configuration
file, and one license notice.

32
00:02:16.923 --> 00:02:21.385
The observed package also contains an
installer and a symbolic

33
00:02:21.385 --> 00:02:25.846
link that points outside the extraction
root. A filename-based check

34
00:02:25.846 --> 00:02:30.308
might accept the familiar shards and
ignore the extras. A

35
00:02:30.308 --> 00:02:34.769
safe acquisition enumerates the complete
observed inventory, rejects traversal and

36
00:02:34.769 --> 00:02:39.231
absolute paths, identifies the symbolic
link as an unsafe surface,

37
00:02:39.231 --> 00:02:43.692
and holds or rejects the candidate
according to policy. The

38
00:02:43.692 --> 00:02:48.154
operator does not load the model to see
whether it

39
00:02:48.154 --> 00:02:52.615
works. The mismatch itself is sufficient
to block promotion while

40
00:02:52.615 --> 00:02:57.077
the original manifest, bytes, observed
digests, timestamp, and verifier output

41
00:02:57.077 --> 00:03:01.538
are preserved. This is a pre-execution
decision. It does not

42
00:03:01.538 --> 00:03:06.000
depend on a successful inference test.

43
00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:10.333
Verification signals answer different
questions, so do not collapse them

44
00:03:10.333 --> 00:03:14.667
into one trust badge. A SHA-256 digest
establishes equality between

45
00:03:14.667 --> 00:03:19.000
observed bytes and an expected digest. It
does not establish

46
00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:23.333
publisher identity, provenance, licensing,
safe loading, acceptable behavior, or

47
00:03:23.333 --> 00:03:27.667
model quality. A cryptographic signature
can bind signed material to

48
00:03:27.667 --> 00:03:32.000
an identity under a verification policy.
Signature validity alone does

49
00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:36.333
not establish that the signer is
authorized for this artifact,

50
00:03:36.333 --> 00:03:40.667
that the signed bytes satisfy deployment
policy, or that behavior

51
00:03:40.667 --> 00:03:45.000
is safe. This lesson includes no
production public key, certificate

52
00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:49.333
chain, transparency-log check, or
signature implementation. If production

53
00:03:49.333 --> 00:03:53.667
requires a signature and it is absent, the
result is

54
00:03:53.667 --> 00:03:58.000
hold. The fixture's not-applicable status
is allowed only under a

55
00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:02.333
narrow local unsigned-fixture policy. SLSA
provenance describes how an artifact

56
00:04:02.333 --> 00:04:06.667
was produced, including relevant inputs
and build information. Its source,

57
00:04:06.667 --> 00:04:11.000
builder, configuration, and predicates
must be authenticated and checked against

58
00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:15.333
policy. A candidate-controlled manifest
that merely repeats expected strings is

59
00:04:15.333 --> 00:04:19.667
not authenticated provenance. Scans report
findings only within their configured

60
00:04:19.667 --> 00:04:24.000
rules, inputs, and coverage. A clean
result means no covered

61
00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:28.333
finding was reported. It does not prove
that malicious behavior,

62
00:04:28.333 --> 00:04:32.667
unsafe deserialization, model-level
failure, an uncovered vulnerability, or

63
00:04:32.667 --> 00:04:37.000
unacceptable terms are absent. A software
bill of materials inventories

64
00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:41.333
declared components and relationships. It
does not prove behavior, licensing

65
00:04:41.333 --> 00:04:45.667
approval, or complete security coverage.
Each signal is useful, but

66
00:04:45.667 --> 00:04:50.000
each remains bounded.

67
00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:53.667
Checkpoint. A candidate's digest matches
the expected value. What exactly

68
00:04:53.667 --> 00:04:57.333
has been established? Name at least two
important claims that

69
00:04:57.333 --> 00:05:01.000
still need different evidence.

70
00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:20.182
The matching digest establishes byte
equality with the expected digest.

71
00:06:20.182 --> 00:06:24.364
It does not tell you who should have
published those

72
00:06:24.364 --> 00:06:28.545
bytes, how they were built, whether the
terms permit your

73
00:06:28.545 --> 00:06:32.727
use, whether loading is safe, or whether
behavior meets requirements.

74
00:06:32.727 --> 00:06:36.909
If your answer used the word trusted,
narrow it. Say

75
00:06:36.909 --> 00:06:41.091
what is trusted, under which policy, and
what separate evidence

76
00:06:41.091 --> 00:06:45.273
remains necessary. For example, a digest
can show that the

77
00:06:45.273 --> 00:06:49.455
observed bytes equal an independently
trusted expected value. It cannot

78
00:06:49.455 --> 00:06:53.636
turn a candidate-controlled manifest into
authenticated provenance. A correctly

79
00:06:53.636 --> 00:06:57.818
signed artifact also needs signer
authorization, policy checks, and

80
00:06:57.818 --> 00:07:02.000
behavioral evaluation.

81
00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:06.227
Inspect the complete executable and parser
surface before model loading.

82
00:07:06.227 --> 00:07:10.455
A model repository can contain serialized
objects, language modules, native

83
00:07:10.455 --> 00:07:14.682
extensions, build scripts, package
metadata, custom operators, tokenizer

84
00:07:14.682 --> 00:07:18.909
implementations, templates, conversion
tools, and runtime plugins. PyTorch

85
00:07:18.909 --> 00:07:23.136
documents that its loading path uses an
unpickler and warns

86
00:07:23.136 --> 00:07:27.364
against loading data from an untrusted
source. Prefer non-executable tensor

87
00:07:27.364 --> 00:07:31.591
formats when the selected runtime supports
them, but do not

88
00:07:31.591 --> 00:07:35.818
trust a file extension by itself. Inspect
archive traversal, absolute

89
00:07:35.818 --> 00:07:40.045
paths, symbolic links, oversized or
malformed tensors, duplicate entries,

90
00:07:40.045 --> 00:07:44.273
unexpected files, dependency installers,
dynamic imports, network calls,

91
00:07:44.273 --> 00:07:48.500
custom-code flags, templates, tokenizer
behavior, and conversion steps. The

92
00:07:48.500 --> 00:07:52.727
supplied verifier rejects unsafe paths,
duplicate inventory entries, links, path

93
00:07:52.727 --> 00:07:56.955
escape after realpath resolution, missing
or unlisted files, malformed evidence,

94
00:07:56.955 --> 00:08:01.182
size mismatches, digest mismatches,
incomplete software bill of materials

95
00:08:01.182 --> 00:08:05.409
coverage, and executable-surface
declarations outside the fixture policy.

96
00:08:05.409 --> 00:08:09.636
It enumerates only the bounded fixtures
directory, so lesson source

97
00:08:09.636 --> 00:08:13.864
and test files are not mistaken for
artifacts. If a

98
00:08:13.864 --> 00:08:18.091
parser or converter is unavoidable, run it
in a disposable

99
00:08:18.091 --> 00:08:22.318
least-privileged sandbox with strict
network, CPU, memory, process, file-count,

100
00:08:22.318 --> 00:08:26.545
time, and storage limits. These controls
reduce known risks. They

101
00:08:26.545 --> 00:08:30.773
do not prove that a real parser, inference
engine, accelerator

102
00:08:30.773 --> 00:08:35.000
library, tokenizer, or model is safe.

103
00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:39.059
Conversion, merging, pruning,
quantization, sharding, repackaging, or

104
00:08:39.059 --> 00:08:43.118
changing a tokenizer or template creates a
materially different deployment

105
00:08:43.118 --> 00:08:47.176
artifact. Record input identities and
digests, tool and dependency versions,

106
00:08:47.176 --> 00:08:51.235
configuration, command or workflow,
isolated environment, output inventory and

107
00:08:51.235 --> 00:08:55.294
digests, operator or automation identity,
and the new evaluation target.

108
00:08:55.294 --> 00:08:59.353
The supplied synthetic lineage record
names input fixture-source-v1, uses the

109
00:08:59.353 --> 00:09:03.412
empty-file digest, performs
synthetic-quantize with fixture-tool

110
00:09:03.412 --> 00:09:07.471
version 0.1, and records bits equal to 8
and group

111
00:09:07.471 --> 00:09:11.529
size equal to 32. Its output identity is
fixture-quantized-v1, but

112
00:09:11.529 --> 00:09:15.588
its output digest is UNKNOWN. That missing
digest is deliberately

113
00:09:15.588 --> 00:09:19.647
not promotable. Actual output bytes, a
measured digest, and independently

114
00:09:19.647 --> 00:09:23.706
checked toolchain evidence would establish
the missing value. The evaluation

115
00:09:23.706 --> 00:09:27.765
boundary is the transformed artifact on
its target runtime, not

116
00:09:27.765 --> 00:09:31.824
the source artifact. Repeat integrity,
license, compatibility,

117
00:09:31.824 --> 00:09:35.882
executable-surface, resource, and
behavioral evaluation gates for the

118
00:09:35.882 --> 00:09:39.941
transformed artifact. Approval cannot be
inherited merely because approved input

119
00:09:39.941 --> 00:09:44.000
weights began the process.

120
00:09:44.000 --> 00:09:48.346
Promotion is a controlled state
transition, not a rename. A

121
00:09:48.346 --> 00:09:52.692
promoted bundle identifies exact weights,
tokenizer, template, configuration,

122
00:09:52.692 --> 00:09:57.038
runtime, dependencies, policy, file
digests, signature status, provenance,

123
00:09:57.038 --> 00:10:01.385
scans, software bill of materials, license
disposition, compatibility results,

124
00:10:01.385 --> 00:10:05.731
evaluation target, reviewer decisions, and
expiry triggers. Store or reference

125
00:10:05.731 --> 00:10:10.077
it by immutable identity. Configure
serving by that identity rather

126
00:10:10.077 --> 00:10:14.423
than by a mutable alias. In the supplied
fixture policy,

127
00:10:14.423 --> 00:10:18.769
a narrow test promotion can pass for inert
static bytes,

128
00:10:18.769 --> 00:10:23.115
serving disabled, bounded file count and
size, complete filesystem inventory,

129
00:10:23.115 --> 00:10:27.462
exact software bill of materials coverage,
explicit not-applicable signature status,

130
00:10:27.462 --> 00:10:31.808
expected local source and builder fields,
stated scan scope, no

131
00:10:31.808 --> 00:10:36.154
custom code, and no attempted load. That
is a genuine

132
00:10:36.154 --> 00:10:40.500
local state transition, not approval of a
real model or

133
00:10:40.500 --> 00:10:44.846
production deployment. Digest equality,
bounded inventory, software bill of

134
00:10:44.846 --> 00:10:49.192
materials equality, expected fixture
provenance, stated scan evidence, and safe

135
00:10:49.192 --> 00:10:53.538
fixture surfaces can pass. A required
production signature that is

136
00:10:53.538 --> 00:10:57.885
missing must hold while an authorized
verifier checks the signature,

137
00:10:57.885 --> 00:11:02.231
signed subject, key or certificate trust,
revocation status, and policy

138
00:11:02.231 --> 00:11:06.577
authorization. Path escape, malformed
evidence, unsafe deserialization,

139
00:11:06.577 --> 00:11:10.923
resource-limit violation, unlisted
content, digest mismatch, or policy

140
00:11:10.923 --> 00:11:15.269
mismatch must reject. On rejection,
preserve the original manifest, rejected

141
00:11:15.269 --> 00:11:19.615
bytes, observed digests, verifier output,
timestamp, and operator identity in

142
00:11:19.615 --> 00:11:23.962
immutable or content-addressed evidence.
Mark the candidate revoked, block serving

143
00:11:23.962 --> 00:11:28.308
and controlled mirrors, investigate
affected environments, and restore only

144
00:11:28.308 --> 00:11:32.654
the last verified immutable identity. Do
not delete rejected evidence

145
00:11:32.654 --> 00:11:37.000
or change the expected digest to fit the
candidate.

146
00:11:37.000 --> 00:11:41.231
Now design the synthetic artifact
promotion packet. Use only the

147
00:11:41.231 --> 00:11:45.462
supplied inert fixture. Describe the
quarantine boundary, pinned source

148
00:11:45.462 --> 00:11:49.692
revision, exact inventory, SHA-256 policy,
signature policy, provenance expectations,

149
00:11:49.692 --> 00:11:53.923
scan scope, software bill of materials,
dependency review, executable-surface

150
00:11:53.923 --> 00:11:58.154
review, file and resource caps, and
unsafe-deserialization stop conditions.

151
00:11:58.154 --> 00:12:02.385
Add the synthetic quantization lineage
record, including its new input

152
00:12:02.385 --> 00:12:06.615
identity, operation, toolchain,
configuration, output identity, UNKNOWN

153
00:12:06.615 --> 00:12:10.846
output digest, and new evaluation
boundary. Then write explicit pass,

154
00:12:10.846 --> 00:12:15.077
hold, and reject rules. Finish with an
immutable promotion manifest

155
00:12:15.077 --> 00:12:19.308
and a recovery procedure that preserves
rejected evidence, blocks the

156
00:12:19.308 --> 00:12:23.538
candidate, and restores the last verified
identity. This packet is

157
00:12:23.538 --> 00:12:27.769
documentation and local fixture work. Do
not download, load, deserialize,

158
00:12:27.769 --> 00:12:32.000
convert, execute, or serve a real model.

159
00:15:32.000 --> 00:15:36.243
We now work through the supplied verifier.
The fixed inventory

160
00:15:36.243 --> 00:15:40.486
contains an empty inert file at fixtures
slash artifact dot

161
00:15:40.486 --> 00:15:44.730
bin and a tokenizer file at fixtures slash
tokenizer dot

162
00:15:44.730 --> 00:15:48.973
txt containing exactly three bytes: abc.
The verifier reads bytes

163
00:15:48.973 --> 00:15:53.216
and metadata only. It does not download,
deserialize, execute, convert,

164
00:15:53.216 --> 00:15:57.459
or serve a model. It first validates
manifest structure, trusted

165
00:15:57.459 --> 00:16:01.703
local fixture-policy expectations, safe
paths, complete filesystem enumeration,

166
00:16:01.703 --> 00:16:05.946
file sizes, SHA-256 digests, software bill
of materials equality, executable-surface

167
00:16:05.946 --> 00:16:10.189
declarations, signature disposition,
provenance fields, and scan scope. The

168
00:16:10.189 --> 00:16:14.432
starter's one deliberate defect occurs
only at the final transition.

169
00:16:14.432 --> 00:16:18.676
Earlier gates have already passed, but the
final comparison uses

170
00:16:18.676 --> 00:16:22.919
the bundle label instead of the manifest's
exact promotion inventory

171
00:16:22.919 --> 00:16:27.162
binding. A bundle label identifies the
packet. The inventory binding

172
00:16:27.162 --> 00:16:31.405
identifies the complete verified
path-and-digest inventory. Those are

173
00:16:31.405 --> 00:16:35.649
different facts. Repair only the marked
expression in verify dot

174
00:16:35.649 --> 00:16:39.892
mjs. Replace manifest dot bundle ID with
manifest dot promotion

175
00:16:39.892 --> 00:16:44.135
dot inventory binding. Do not hardcode
either fixture digest, bypass

176
00:16:44.135 --> 00:16:48.378
a failed gate, trust a filename as proof,
edit immutable

177
00:16:48.378 --> 00:16:52.622
tests, edit the shared verifier core, or
reject every input.

178
00:16:52.622 --> 00:16:56.865
The supplied starter output ends with
promotion reject,

179
00:16:56.865 --> 00:17:01.108
inventory-binding-mismatch, expected
local-fixture-v1, followed by the complete

180
00:17:01.108 --> 00:17:05.351
canonical inventory binding. After the
narrow repair, the baseline exits

181
00:17:05.351 --> 00:17:09.595
zero and ends with promotion pass, bundle
equals local-fixture-v1. The

182
00:17:09.595 --> 00:17:13.838
important causal point is that all
previous evidence was valid.

183
00:17:13.838 --> 00:17:18.081
The final identity binding alone was
wrong. Node's file URL

184
00:17:18.081 --> 00:17:22.324
to path function converts the module URL
to a platform-appropriate

185
00:17:22.324 --> 00:17:26.568
filesystem path. Web crypto subtle digest
computes SHA-256 over bytes.

186
00:17:26.568 --> 00:17:30.811
Path relative supports containment checks,
and file-system lstat identifies symbolic

187
00:17:30.811 --> 00:17:35.054
links. The reference uses an explicit
workspace argument as supplied.

188
00:17:35.054 --> 00:17:39.297
Its default is the parent of its reference
directory, correcting

189
00:17:39.297 --> 00:17:43.541
the earlier defect that moved every
explicit workspace to its

190
00:17:43.541 --> 00:17:47.784
parent. The exact root-relative commands
are shown visually, not spoken:

191
00:17:47.784 --> 00:17:52.027
node training slash
self-hosted-model-operations slash

192
00:17:52.027 --> 00:17:56.270
model-artifact-integrity slash lab slash
verify dot mjs, and node training

193
00:17:56.270 --> 00:18:00.514
slash self-hosted-model-operations slash
model-artifact-integrity slash lab slash

194
00:18:00.514 --> 00:18:04.757
tests dot mjs. The command must be run
from the

195
00:18:04.757 --> 00:18:09.000
repository root.

196
00:18:09.000 --> 00:18:13.500
Your first changed-input task is a
same-length tamper test. Change

197
00:18:13.500 --> 00:18:18.000
the tokenizer contents from abc to abd,
keeping the file

198
00:18:18.000 --> 00:18:22.500
size at three bytes. Leave the expected
baseline manifest unchanged.

199
00:18:22.500 --> 00:18:27.000
Before viewing the answer, predict which
gate should reject, why

200
00:18:27.000 --> 00:18:31.500
the size gate should not reject first, and
what digest

201
00:18:31.500 --> 00:18:36.000
evidence should appear. Then distinguish
this from a trusted changed-input

202
00:18:36.000 --> 00:18:40.500
test, where a copied manifest and complete
promotion binding are

203
00:18:40.500 --> 00:18:45.000
deliberately updated to the independently
calculated new digest.

204
00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:04.353
The changed bytes are abd, still three
bytes long. The

205
00:20:04.353 --> 00:20:08.706
independently calculated digest is
displayed. The unchanged baseline digest

206
00:20:08.706 --> 00:20:13.059
is also displayed. Because the size
remains three, the size

207
00:20:13.059 --> 00:20:17.412
gate passes. The digest gate then rejects
the changed bytes.

208
00:20:17.412 --> 00:20:21.765
The output reports digest reject for the
tokenizer path and

209
00:20:21.765 --> 00:20:26.118
promotion reject for digest mismatch. A
separate size test writes

210
00:20:26.118 --> 00:20:30.471
one byte to an empty file. It expects size

211
00:20:30.471 --> 00:20:34.824
mismatch before digest comparison. Do not
confuse those causes. The

212
00:20:34.824 --> 00:20:39.176
trusted changed-input variation is
different. It copies the test manifest,

213
00:20:39.176 --> 00:20:43.529
calculates the new digest independently,
updates the inventory digest, and

214
00:20:43.529 --> 00:20:47.882
updates the complete promotion inventory
binding. That variation passes the

215
00:20:47.882 --> 00:20:52.235
narrow local fixture policy. This shows
the verifier is not

216
00:20:52.235 --> 00:20:56.588
hardcoded to the original hashes. It does
not show that

217
00:20:56.588 --> 00:21:00.941
a candidate-controlled production manifest
is trustworthy. A deny-all implementation

218
00:21:00.941 --> 00:21:05.294
would also be wrong. It would reject valid
changed input.

219
00:21:05.294 --> 00:21:09.647
A hardcoded allowlist would also be wrong.
It would fail

220
00:21:09.647 --> 00:21:14.000
the independently updated trusted
